# Phosphor Mono 8x16 — RetroOS text-mode font
# (C) RetroOS contributors. Original drawing. License: SIL OFL 1.1.
#
# Format:  "@ <hex codepoint> <name> [+<first row>]"  followed by rows of
# exactly 8 cells ('#' = ink, '.' = paper). Rows before <first row> and after
# the last given row are blank. Cell is 8x16; glyph ink lives in columns 0-6,
# column 7 is inter-character space.
#
# Metrics: cap height rows 2-11, x-height rows 5-11, baseline under row 11,
# descenders rows 12-14, row 15 is always blank (the underline cursor lives there).
# Box drawing (U+2500-257F), blocks (U+2580-259F) and accented Latin-1 letters
# are generated from rules in retro-gfx (font/synth.rs), not drawn here.

